# A config that imports `Lean`, which the editor's base does not hold. The
# gate runs it stepped, as every fixture of tests/headless; the benchmarks
# (tools/module-bench.sh, tools/bundle-bench.sh) run it from a staged
# bundle, with no directory argument, an empty environment and a working
# directory outside the bundle, so the config in `config/` is elaborated on
# the modules the bundle holds. What it prints must be exactly `expected`.

# This settle waits up to 90 s, three times the default 30 s: a cold,
# interpreted elaboration of a config that imports `Lean`, which from a
# staged bundle reads about 1.3 GB of module files just copied there. A
# reload that never ends still fails here, naming this line and the
# 90000 ms.
reload
settle 90000

# `squares` is config's: it runs interpreted, calling compiled code of
# `Init` and of `Editor`. Text 0 is the scratch buffer's.
run squares
show
